// error
// SPEC §10.5, #5051: the synthesised member is written in terms of
// `FieldDesc` and `AttrDesc`, so the module has to have them in scope.
// Reported ONCE, naming the import to add, INSTEAD of synthesising -- a
// member emitted here would produce a cascade of undefined-name errors on a
// signature the user never wrote, every one of them pointing at the class
// header.
@table class User {
  id: i64,
}

fn main() {
  print("${User{ id: 1 }.id}\n")
}
